module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Abelian
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Colimits
public import StacksCore.CategoryTheory.GradedObject.Abelian
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.GenSetCechColimit

/-!
# The complex `K(A, I)` as a complex of presheaves of modules over the rings carrying a family

Fix `r : ℕ`. A **generated pair** is a commutative ring `A` together with a family
`f₁, …, f_r ∈ A`; its ideal is `I = (f₁, …, f_r)`, which is finitely generated by construction.
A morphism of generated pairs is a ring map carrying the family *pointwise* to the family, so the
ideal of the target is the image of the ideal of the source and the category of generated pairs
comes with a structure presheaf of rings `A` and the ideal as a subpresheaf.

This is exactly the shape in which [Stacks, Tag 099E] meets [Stacks, Tag 099D]: on the slice site
`𝒞/U` of a ringed site with `ℐ|_U` generated by `f₁, …, f_r ∈ ℐ(U)`, the assignment
`V/U ↦ (𝒪(V), f₁|_V, …, f_r|_V)` is a functor to the generated pairs, because the restriction of
the generating family *is* the generating family of `I𝒪(V)`, on the nose.

On this category the filtered colimit of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/GenSetCechColimit.lean` assembles into one **complex of presheaves
of modules**

`K^n(X) = colim_{S ∈ GenSet A I} Č^n(A, fam S)`,   `X = (A, f₁, …, f_r)`,

with an augmentation onto the structure presheaf in degree zero. Its restriction maps are the
descended transports, which compose on the nose, so this is a presheaf of modules and not merely
a family of complexes with comparisons. The value at `X` mentions only the ring and the ideal of
`X`, not the chosen family, which is the content of "`K` depends only on the pair".

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair` — the category of generated pairs, with `Stacks.GenPairSite.ideal`
  its ideal, `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair.theGen` the chosen family read as an element of
  `Stacks.GenFamily.Gen`, and `Stacks.GenPairSite.ringFunctor`,
  `Stacks.GenPairSite.structureRings` the structure presheaf of rings.
* `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPairModule` — presheaves of modules on the generated pairs, with
  `Stacks.GenPairSite.evaluation` and `Stacks.GenPairSite.structureModule`.
* `Stacks.GenPairSite.kTerm`, `Stacks.GenPairSite.kDiff`, `Stacks.GenPairSite.kComplexNat` —
  **the complex of presheaves of modules**, degreewise the filtered colimit.
* `Stacks.GenPairSite.kAugZero` — its augmentation onto the structure presheaf.
* `Stacks.GenPairSite.sectionsNat`, `Stacks.GenPairSite.sectionsLegNat` — the complex of sections
  at an object, and the leg of the colimit at one index.

## Main results

* `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair.Hom.map_ideal` — a morphism carries the ideal onto the ideal.
* `Stacks.GenPairSite.isColimit_sectionsCoconeNat` — **the sections at an object are the filtered
  colimit** of the Čech complexes of the product families.
* `Stacks.GenPairSite.quasiIso_sectionsLegNat` — **each leg of that colimit is a
  quasi-isomorphism**: the diagram is filtered and all its transitions are.

## Implementation notes

The value of a presheaf of modules at `X` is an object of `ModuleCat ↑(structureRings.obj X)`
while every Čech construction produces an object of `ModuleCat X.ring`. The two categories are
definitionally equal but not syntactically so, and `rw`, `simp` and instance search all work
below the transparency at which they become equal; as in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/PairCechColimit.lean`, everything below names the `ModuleCat X.ring`
spelling.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached here: the complex of this file is the presheaf-level model
whose comparison with a single Čech complex is proved in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/GenPairCechPresheaf.lean`, and no clause of a tag is settled by the
construction alone.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.GenPairSite

open Stacks.GenFamily

/-! ### The category of generated pairs -/

/-- **A generated pair**: a commutative ring together with a chosen family of `r` of its
elements. The ideal it generates is finitely generated by construction, so no finiteness
hypothesis is ever carried. -/
structure GenPair (r : ℕ) : Type (u + 1) where
  /-- The underlying ring. -/
  ring : Type u
  /-- Its commutative ring structure. -/
  commRing : CommRing ring
  /-- The chosen family of `r` elements. -/
  elts : Fin r → ring

attribute [instance] GenPair.commRing

variable {r : ℕ}

/-- **The ideal of a generated pair**: the ideal generated by the chosen family. -/
def ideal (P : GenPair.{u} r) : Ideal P.ring := Ideal.span (Set.range P.elts)

/-- The ideal of a generated pair is finitely generated: it is generated by a finite family. -/
theorem ideal_fg (P : GenPair.{u} r) : (ideal P).FG :=
  Submodule.fg_iff_exists_fin_generating_family.2 ⟨r, P.elts, rfl⟩

/-- The chosen family of a generated pair, read as a finite generating family of its ideal. -/
def GenPair.theGen (P : GenPair.{u} r) : Gen P.ring (ideal P) := ⟨r, P.elts, rfl⟩

/-- The generating family `GenPair.theGen P` has arity `r`. -/
@[simp]
theorem GenPair.theGen_arity (P : GenPair.{u} r) : P.theGen.arity = r := rfl

/-- The elements of `GenPair.theGen P` are the chosen family of `P`. -/
@[simp]
theorem GenPair.theGen_elts (P : GenPair.{u} r) : P.theGen.elts = P.elts := rfl

/-- **A morphism of generated pairs**: a ring map carrying the chosen family pointwise onto the
chosen family, with the equalities holding on the nose. -/
structure GenPair.Hom (P Q : GenPair.{u} r) where
  /-- The underlying ring map. -/
  toRingHom : P.ring →+* Q.ring
  /-- It carries the chosen family onto the chosen family. -/
  map_elts : ∀ i : Fin r, toRingHom (P.elts i) = Q.elts i

/-- A morphism of generated pairs is determined by its underlying ring map. -/
theorem GenPair.Hom.ext' {P Q : GenPair.{u} r} :
    ∀ {f g : GenPair.Hom P Q}, f.toRingHom = g.toRingHom → f = g
  | ⟨_, _⟩, ⟨_, _⟩, rfl => rfl

/-- **The category of generated pairs.** It is locally small: the morphisms between two objects
form a `Type u`. -/
instance : Category.{u, u + 1} (GenPair.{u} r) where
  Hom P Q := GenPair.Hom P Q
  id P := ⟨RingHom.id P.ring, fun _ => rfl⟩
  comp {_ _ _} f g :=
    ⟨g.toRingHom.comp f.toRingHom, fun i => by
      rw [RingHom.comp_apply, f.map_elts, g.map_elts]⟩
  id_comp f := GenPair.Hom.ext' (RingHom.comp_id f.toRingHom)
  comp_id f := GenPair.Hom.ext' (RingHom.id_comp f.toRingHom)
  assoc f g h := GenPair.Hom.ext' (RingHom.comp_assoc f.toRingHom g.toRingHom h.toRingHom).symm

/-- The ring map underlying the identity of a generated pair is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem id_toRingHom (P : GenPair.{u} r) :
    GenPair.Hom.toRingHom (𝟙 P) = RingHom.id P.ring := rfl

/-- The ring map underlying a composite of morphisms of generated pairs is the composite of the
underlying ring maps. -/
@[simp]
theorem comp_toRingHom {P Q S : GenPair.{u} r} (f : P ⟶ Q) (g : Q ⟶ S) :
    (f ≫ g).toRingHom = g.toRingHom.comp f.toRingHom := rfl

/-- **A morphism of generated pairs carries the ideal of the source onto the ideal of the
target.** -/
theorem GenPair.Hom.map_ideal {P Q : GenPair.{u} r} (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    ideal Q = Ideal.map (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f) (ideal P) := by
  have h : (fun i => (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f) (P.elts i)) = Q.elts :=
    funext (GenPair.Hom.map_elts f)
  rw [ideal, ideal, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
  exact congrArg (fun g : Fin r → Q.ring => Ideal.span (Set.range g)) h.symm

/-- **The image of the chosen family is the chosen family**, as generating families. -/
theorem GenPair.map_theGen {P Q : GenPair.{u} r} (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    Gen.map (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f) (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal f) P.theGen = Q.theGen := by
  have key : ∀ (g : Fin r → Q.ring) (hg : Ideal.span (Set.range g) = ideal Q)
      (g' : Fin r → Q.ring) (hg' : Ideal.span (Set.range g') = ideal Q), g = g' →
      (⟨r, g, hg⟩ : Gen Q.ring (ideal Q)) = ⟨r, g', hg'⟩ := by
    intro g hg g' hg' hgg
    subst hgg
    rfl
  exact key _ _ _ _ (funext (GenPair.Hom.map_elts f))

/-! ### The structure presheaf of rings -/

/-- An object of the category of generated pairs, read as an index for the values of a presheaf
on the site of generated pairs: the site is `(GenPair r)ᵒᵖ`, so presheaves on it are indexed by
`(GenPair r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ`. -/
abbrev GenPair.ix (P : GenPair.{u} r) : (GenPair.{u} r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ := op (op P)

/-- A morphism of generated pairs, read as a morphism of indices for a presheaf. It goes the same
way: a presheaf on `(GenPair r)ᵒᵖ` is a *covariant* functor on generated pairs. -/
abbrev GenPair.Hom.ix {P Q : GenPair.{u} r} (f : P ⟶ Q) : P.ix ⟶ Q.ix := (Quiver.Hom.op f).op

/-- **The ring of a generated pair, functorially.** -/
def ringFunctor (r : ℕ) : GenPair.{u} r ⥤ RingCat.{u} where
  obj P := RingCat.of P.ring
  map f := RingCat.ofHom f.toRingHom
  map_id _ := rfl
  map_comp _ _ := rfl

/-- **The structure presheaf of rings on the site of generated pairs**, in the form Mathlib's
`PresheafOfModules` consumes. -/
def structureRings (r : ℕ) : (GenPair.{u} r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  unopUnop (GenPair.{u} r) ⋙ ringFunctor.{u} r

/-- The value of the structure presheaf of rings at a generated pair is its ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem structureRings_obj (P : GenPair.{u} r) :
    (structureRings.{u} r).obj P.ix = RingCat.of P.ring := rfl

/-- The structure presheaf of rings sends a morphism of generated pairs to its underlying ring
map. -/
@[simp]
theorem structureRings_map {P Q : GenPair.{u} r} (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    ((structureRings.{u} r).map (GenPair.Hom.ix f)).hom = f.toRingHom := rfl

/-! ### Presheaves of modules on the site of generated pairs -/

/-- **A presheaf of modules on the category of generated pairs.** -/
abbrev GenPairModule (r : ℕ) := PresheafOfModules.{u} (structureRings.{u} r)

/-- The value of a presheaf of modules on generated pairs at an object. -/
abbrev GenPairModule.value (M : GenPairModule.{u} r) (P : GenPair.{u} r) :
    ModuleCat.{u} P.ring :=
  M.obj P.ix

/-- **Evaluation at a generated pair.** -/
abbrev evaluation (P : GenPair.{u} r) : GenPairModule.{u} r ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} P.ring :=
  PresheafOfModules.evaluation (structureRings.{u} r) P.ix

/-- Evaluation at a generated pair is additive. This is `PresheafOfModules.evaluation`'s own
instance, restated with the target written as `ModuleCat P.ring` rather than as
`ModuleCat ↑(structureRings.obj P.ix)`. -/
instance instAdditiveEvaluation (P : GenPair.{u} r) : (evaluation.{u} P).Additive :=
  inferInstanceAs ((PresheafOfModules.evaluation (structureRings.{u} r) P.ix).Additive)

/-- Evaluation at a generated pair preserves zero morphisms. -/
instance instPreservesZeroMorphismsEvaluation (P : GenPair.{u} r) :
    (evaluation.{u} P).PreservesZeroMorphisms :=
  Functor.preservesZeroMorphisms_of_additive _

/-- **The structure presheaf, as a presheaf of modules over itself.** -/
abbrev structureModule (r : ℕ) : GenPairModule.{u} r :=
  PresheafOfModules.unit (structureRings.{u} r)

/-! ### The complex of presheaves of modules -/

/-- **The degree-`n` term of the complex of presheaves of modules**: at the object `X` the
filtered colimit, over the finite sets of finite generating families of the ideal of `X`, of the
degree-`n` Čech terms of their product families. The value mentions only the ring and the ideal
of `X`. -/
def kTerm (n : ℕ) : GenPairModule.{u} r where
  obj X := (colimit (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram (X.unop.unop).ring (ideal X.unop.unop) n) :
    ModuleCat.{u} (X.unop.unop).ring)
  map {_ _} f :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop) n
  map_id X := GenSetCech.transportDesc_id (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal (𝟙 (X.unop.unop))) n
  map_comp {_ _ _} f g :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc_comp (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom g.unop.unop) (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop)
      (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal g.unop.unop)
      (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal (f.unop.unop ≫ g.unop.unop)) n

/-- The value of `kTerm n` at `X` is the filtered colimit of the degree-`n` Čech terms. -/
@[simp]
theorem kTerm_obj (n : ℕ) (X : (GenPair.{u} r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ) :
    (kTerm.{u} (r := r) n).obj X =
      colimit (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram (X.unop.unop).ring (ideal X.unop.unop) n) := rfl

/-- The restriction map of `kTerm n` along a morphism is the map of colimits induced by
transporting generating families along the underlying ring map. -/
@[simp]
theorem kTerm_map (n : ℕ) {X Y : (GenPair.{u} r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (kTerm.{u} (r := r) n).map f =
      GenSetCech.transportDesc (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
        (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop) n := rfl

/-- **The differential of the complex of presheaves of modules.** -/
def kDiff (n : ℕ) : kTerm.{u} (r := r) n ⟶ kTerm.{u} (r := r) (n + 1) where
  app X := GenSetCech.diffDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (ideal X.unop.unop) n
  naturality {_ _} f :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc_comp_diffDesc (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop) n

/-- The component of `kDiff n` at `X` is the colimit of the Čech differentials. -/
@[simp]
theorem kDiff_app (n : ℕ) (X : (GenPair.{u} r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (kDiff.{u} (r := r) n) X =
      GenSetCech.diffDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (ideal X.unop.unop) n := rfl

/-- **The complex of presheaves of modules of [Stacks, Tag 099D], in nonnegative degrees.** -/
def kComplexNat (r : ℕ) : CochainComplex (GenPairModule.{u} r) ℕ :=
  CochainComplex.of kTerm.{u} kDiff.{u} fun n =>
    PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun X =>
      GenSetCech.diffDesc_comp_diffDesc (A := (X.unop.unop).ring) (I := ideal X.unop.unop) n

/-- The degree-`n` term of `kComplexNat r` is `kTerm n`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kComplexNat_X (n : ℕ) : (kComplexNat.{u} r).X n = kTerm.{u} (r := r) n := rfl

/-- The differential of `kComplexNat r` from degree `n` to degree `n + 1` is `kDiff n`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kComplexNat_d (n : ℕ) :
    (kComplexNat.{u} r).d n (n + 1) = kDiff.{u} (r := r) n :=
  CochainComplex.of_d _ _ n

/-- **The augmentation of the degree-zero term onto the structure presheaf.** -/
def kAugZero (r : ℕ) : kTerm.{u} (r := r) 0 ⟶ structureModule.{u} r where
  app X := GenSetCech.augDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (ideal X.unop.unop)
  naturality {_ _} f :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc_comp_augDesc (GenPair.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (GenPair.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop)

/-- The component of `kAugZero r` at `X` is the colimit of the Čech augmentations. -/
@[simp]
theorem kAugZero_app (X : (GenPair.{u} r)ᵒᵖᵒᵖ) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (kAugZero.{u} r) X =
      GenSetCech.augDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (ideal X.unop.unop) := rfl

/-! ### The sections at an object are the filtered colimit -/

/-- **The complex of sections of the complex of presheaves of modules at an object**, written
over the object's own ring. -/
abbrev sectionsNat (P : GenPair.{u} r) : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} P.ring) ℕ :=
  ((evaluation P).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj (kComplexNat.{u} r)

/-- The differential of `sectionsNat P` from degree `n` to degree `n + 1` is the colimit of the
Čech differentials of `P.ring` and `ideal P`. -/
theorem sectionsNat_d (P : GenPair.{u} r) (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionsNat P).d n (n + 1) = GenSetCech.diffDesc P.ring (ideal P) n :=
  congrArg (fun w => (evaluation P).map w) (kComplexNat_d.{u} (r := r) n)

/-- **The sections at an object, as a cocone** on the filtered diagram of Čech complexes. -/
def sectionsCoconeNat (P : GenPair.{u} r) :
    Cocone (GenSetCech.cechDiagram P.ring (ideal P)) where
  pt := sectionsNat P
  ι :=
    { app := fun S =>
        { f := fun n => colimit.ι (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring (ideal P) n) S
          comm' := fun n m hnm => by
            obtain rfl : n + 1 = m := hnm
            exact Eq.trans (congrArg
              (fun w => colimit.ι (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring (ideal P) n) S ≫ w)
              (sectionsNat_d P n)) (GenSetCech.ι_diffDesc n S) }
      naturality := fun S T h =>
        HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n =>
          (colimit.w (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring (ideal P) n) h).trans
            (Category.comp_id _).symm }

/-- **The leg of the sections cocone at one generating index**, with its target written as
`Stacks.GenPairSite.sectionsNat` rather than as the value at `S` of a constant functor. -/
def sectionsLegNat (P : GenPair.{u} r) (S : GenSet P.ring (ideal P)) :
    Cech.cechComplex (fam S) P.ring ⟶ sectionsNat P :=
  (sectionsCoconeNat P).ι.app S

/-- In each degree, the leg `sectionsLegNat P S` is the colimit inclusion at `S`. -/
@[simp]
theorem sectionsLegNat_f (P : GenPair.{u} r) (S : GenSet P.ring (ideal P)) (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionsLegNat P S).f n =
      colimit.ι (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring (ideal P) n) S := rfl

/-- **The sections at an object are the colimit of the filtered diagram.** -/
def isColimit_sectionsCoconeNat (P : GenPair.{u} r) : IsColimit (sectionsCoconeNat P) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.isColimitOfEval _ _ fun n => ?_
  exact IsColimit.ofIsoColimit
    (colimit.isColimit (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring (ideal P) n))
    (Cocone.ext (Iso.refl _) fun S => Category.comp_id _)

/-- **Each leg of the colimit is a quasi-isomorphism.** The index system is filtered, the ideal
being finitely generated, and every transition of the diagram is a quasi-isomorphism. -/
theorem quasiIso_sectionsLegNat (P : GenPair.{u} r) (S : GenSet P.ring (ideal P)) :
    QuasiIso (sectionsLegNat P S) :=
  have := GenSet.isFiltered (ideal_fg P)
  StacksDraft.quasiIso_isColimit_ι (GenSetCech.cechDiagram P.ring (ideal P))
    (fun _ _ h => GenSetCech.quasiIso_cechDiagram_map h) (sectionsCoconeNat P)
    (isColimit_sectionsCoconeNat P) S

end Stacks.GenPairSite

end
